## AggregateExec Partial and Final without GROUP BY
  case default: no violations
  case single partition: no violations
  case inexact statistics: no violations
  case absent statistics: no violations
  case empty input:
    AggregateExec: mode=Final, gby=[], aggr=[count(v), sum(v), min(v), max(v), avg(f), sum(f)]
      CoalescePartitionsExec
        AggregateExec: mode=Partial, gby=[], aggr=[count(v), sum(v), min(v), max(v), avg(f), sum(f)]
          MockSourceExec: partitioning=UnknownPartitioning(3), partition_rows=[0, 0, 0], statistics=Exact
    [invariant] cardinality_effect_bounds_num_rows at AggregateExec (root/0/0): cardinality_effect() is LowerEqual, but num_rows is Exact(3) for an input with num_rows Exact(0)
    [invariant] cardinality_effect_holds at AggregateExec (root/0/0): cardinality_effect() is LowerEqual, but the node produced 3 rows from 0 input rows

