## AggregateExec Single with DISTINCT limit
  allowed batch_boundary_invariance: the limit is a soft limit: the aggregate stops after the input batch in which it has seen 5 groups, so how many and which groups it emits depends on batch boundaries, and only the LIMIT above it makes the result well defined (aggregates/mod.rs:859-864); it reports no fetch, so the check cannot know that
  case default:
    AggregateExec: mode=Single, gby=[g@0 as g], aggr=[], lim=[5]
      MockSourceExec: partitioning=UnknownPartitioning(1), partition_rows=[600], statistics=Exact
    [invariant] exact_statistics_hold at AggregateExec (root): the overall statistics are false: distinct_count of g@0 is Exact(16), but the output has Exact(10)
    [invariant] exact_statistics_hold at AggregateExec (root): the partition 0 statistics are false: distinct_count of g@0 is Exact(16), but the output has Exact(10)
  case single partition:
    AggregateExec: mode=Single, gby=[g@0 as g], aggr=[], lim=[5]
      MockSourceExec: partitioning=UnknownPartitioning(1), partition_rows=[600], statistics=Exact
    [invariant] exact_statistics_hold at AggregateExec (root): the overall statistics are false: distinct_count of g@0 is Exact(16), but the output has Exact(10)
    [invariant] exact_statistics_hold at AggregateExec (root): the partition 0 statistics are false: distinct_count of g@0 is Exact(16), but the output has Exact(10)
  case inexact statistics: no violations
  case absent statistics: no violations
  case empty input: no violations

